WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.020
One protein can pull an axon toward it, and push another axon away.

2
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:13.640
That protein is netrin, a secreted protein that guides growing axons.

3
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:17.680
Here is a growth cone, the moving tip of a growing axon.

4
00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:22.420
Netrin is released from a source on the right, and it thins out with distance.

5
00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.860
Which way will the growth cone turn?

6
00:00:25.733 --> 00:00:28.953
The growth cone reads netrin with receptors on its surface.

7
00:00:29.673 --> 00:00:31.853
One receptor is called DCC.

8
00:00:32.573 --> 00:00:36.693
A growth cone that carries DCC usually turns toward the netrin source.

9
00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:38.133
That is attraction.

10
00:00:38.713 --> 00:00:43.993
In the worm, mutants that lack the relative of DCC fail mainly to move toward the

11
00:00:43.993 --> 00:00:44.993
cue.

12
00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:49.153
Now add a second receptor, called UNC5.

13
00:00:49.893 --> 00:00:56.053
A growth cone that carries DCC and UNC5 usually turns away from the same netrin.

14
00:00:56.633 --> 00:00:57.773
The Q did not change.

15
00:00:58.213 --> 00:00:59.713
Only the receptors changed.

16
00:01:00.273 --> 00:01:06.453
In worms, forcing UNC5 into touch neurons sent their axons away from the Q.

17
00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:08.987
Receptors are only one layer.

18
00:01:09.427 --> 00:01:11.227
The growth cone's interstate is another.

19
00:01:11.727 --> 00:01:15.487
To test it, researchers grew single frog spinal growth cones in a dish.

20
00:01:15.927 --> 00:01:20.407
A fine pipette puffed netrin on one side, and the growth cones turned toward it.

21
00:01:20.907 --> 00:01:24.507
This attraction through DCC needs cyclic AMP signalling.

22
00:01:25.047 --> 00:01:28.247
With that signal on, the growth cone turns toward netrin.

23
00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:30.410
Now block the signal.

24
00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:37.310
Use a competing cyclic AMP analogue, or an inhibitor of protein kinase A. The same

25
00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:39.430
growth cones turn away from the same pipette.

26
00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:43.270
An antibody to DCC stopped both turns.

27
00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:46.010
Both turns needed DCC.

28
00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:50.570
Blocking cyclic AMP signalling changed the direction.

29
00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:53.860
To predict a turn, ask two questions.

30
00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:56.560
Which receptors does the growth cone carry?

31
00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:02.080
DCC usually attracts, and UNC5 receptors usually add repulsion.

32
00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:05.060
And what is its cyclic AMP level?

33
00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:09.480
In frog spinal growth cones, lowering it flips attraction to repulsion.

34
00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:14.500
Treat this as a starting point, because netrin has other receptors and partners too.

35
00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:17.200
Netrin does not decide the turn alone.

36
00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:20.480
The receptors and the interstate decide it.
